If anything in this summary appears to conflict with the binding terms in
Section B, the binding terms control.

================================================================================
SECTION A — DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

"Licensor" means the AFL++ project, acting through its maintainers, in their
capacity as copyright holders of the AGPL-licensed portions of the Covered
Software.

"Covered Software" means the AFL++ software as distributed by the Licensor,
including all first-party files of the project, in source or binary form,
together with any modifications You make.
"Covered Software" does NOT include third-party components that are distributed
under their own separate licenses (for example xxHash, t1ha, libFuzzer, and any
git submodules); those components remain governed solely by their own licenses.

"You" / "Licensee" means the single legal entity that makes (or on whose behalf
is made) a Qualifying Donation, together with that entity's majority-owned
affiliates. A Qualifying Donation covers one Licensee only.

"Qualifying Donation" means a single, genuine, non-refundable charitable
donation of at least EUR 20,000 (twenty thousand euros), or the equivalent in
another currency converted at a publicly available exchange rate on the date of
the donation, made on or after 1 January 2026, by You or on Your behalf and
attributable to You, to EITHER of the following organizations:

  - the Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF), https://www.eff.org/ ; or
  - the Chaos Computer Club (CCC), https://www.ccc.de/ .

A single Qualifying Donation must go entirely to one of those two
organizations; You do not need to donate to both, and splitting the amount
across both does not qualify.

"Proof" means an email sent to afl@aflplus.plus that includes the official
donation receipt or acknowledgment issued by EFF or CCC, clearly showing:
  (a) the recipient organization (EFF or CCC);
  (b) the donated amount;
  (c) the date of the donation; and
  (d) the identity of the donor (You).

"Effective Date" means the calendar date on which the Qualifying Donation was
made, as shown on the Proof.

"Term" means the period of one (1) year beginning on the Effective Date.

